From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Boukje Maria Darago <ik.ben@bouk.je>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:49:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: expose opt-in per-connector MST DDC adapters

An MST chain can expose the physical connector's I2C path without per-display adapters
for the downstream sinks, so ddcutil and KDE PowerDevil can't address each monitor. With
nvidia_drm.mst_ddc=1, register an adapter named DPMST per MST connector and route its
transfers through NVKMS to the DP library's remote I2C sideband messages.

Messages are posted asynchronously: KAPI polls outside the NVKMS and PM locks, so a slow
monitor doesn't block display updates. Requests belong to the DP device and are identified
by unique tokens, callbacks detach the message on completion and failure, and timeouts
cancel it.

Also fixes RemoteI2cReadMessage::parseResponseAck() in the DP library for everyone: the
reply length from the branch device wasn't bounded before filling the 128 byte buffer.

Upstream PR 1400 (Boukje Maria Darago), both commits, on top of the
NVKMS_IOCTL_GET_NEXT_EVENTS addition in this branch. Off by default. Hotplug is known to be
incomplete according to the PR. Not tested here, no MST hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
